WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.747 --> 00:00:18.769
know that Little Joe meant to do his best for me after my exhausting run for the doctor.

2
00:00:19.910 --> 00:00:23.072
But he hadn't been working at the stable long and didn't know much yet.

3
00:00:27.294 --> 00:00:30.276
When he brought me into my stall, I was dripping with sweat.

4
00:00:32.940 --> 00:00:36.843
He rubbed my legs and chest but didn't put anything over me to keep me warm.

5
00:00:38.104 --> 00:00:40.546
He thought I was so warm already that I wouldn't like it.

6
00:00:41.987 --> 00:00:43.748
Then he brought me lots of cold water.

7
00:00:44.468 --> 00:00:47.271
It tasted good when I was hot, so I gulped it all down.

8
00:00:49.592 --> 00:00:52.194
Little Joe thought I must be hungry after working so hard.

9
00:00:52.935 --> 00:00:54.296
He brought me a bucket of corn.

10
00:00:56.637 --> 00:01:00.000
Not long after that, I began to tremble and feel very cold.

11
00:01:01.780 --> 00:01:03.181
My legs and chest ached.

12
00:01:04.022 --> 00:01:05.163
My stomach felt tight.

13
00:01:06.144 --> 00:01:07.405
I was sore all over.

14
00:01:10.268 --> 00:01:11.709
Little Joe had left by then.

15
00:01:12.930 --> 00:01:16.173
I stood there for a long time, wishing I wasn't so cold.

16
00:01:17.314 --> 00:01:19.716
Finally I collapsed onto the straw and tried to sleep.

17
00:01:22.118 --> 00:01:23.799
I woke up when I heard John at the door.

18
00:01:24.920 --> 00:01:28.764
He'd finally finished his long walk home and had come to check on me.

19
00:01:30.104 --> 00:01:31.665
I let out a moan of distress.

20
00:01:32.546 --> 00:01:34.306
John was at my side in an instant.

21
00:01:35.647 --> 00:01:37.408
"Oh, Beauty," he exclaimed.

22
00:01:37.428 --> 00:01:39.870
"What has that stupid boy done?"

23
00:01:41.350 --> 00:01:44.212
I couldn't tell him how bad I felt, but he seemed to know.

24
00:01:45.293 --> 00:01:47.174
He grabbed a blanket and draped it over me.

25
00:01:48.354 --> 00:01:49.855
Then he brought me some warm food.

26
00:01:50.776 --> 00:01:53.837
I felt a little better after I finished it, and I fell asleep.

27
00:01:56.859 --> 00:01:58.660
The next day I was still very sick.

28
00:01:59.836 --> 00:02:02.138
I had a fever and couldn't breathe without pain.

29
00:02:03.779 --> 00:02:08.362
John stayed by my side, and the squire came to my stall to see me several times.

30
00:02:08.382 --> 00:02:11.585
"My poor Beauty," he said.

31
00:02:11.605 --> 00:02:14.667
"You saved your mistress's life, do you know that?

32
00:02:15.968 --> 00:02:19.750
If it had taken the doctor any longer to get here, it would have been too late."

33
00:02:19.770 --> 00:02:24.394
"There was no chance of arriving too late with Beauty," John said.

34
00:02:24.414 --> 00:02:27.496
"I never saw a horse go so fast!

35
00:02:28.436 --> 00:02:30.217
It seemed as if he knew what was wrong!"

36
00:02:31.478 --> 00:02:34.259
Of course I knew, even if John didn't realize it.

37
00:02:35.260 --> 00:02:36.881
Maybe I didn't understand everything.

38
00:02:37.961 --> 00:02:41.643
But I understood that I had to go fast, and that it was for the sake of the

39
00:02:41.683 --> 00:02:48.667
mistress. I'm not sure how many days passed while I was sick.

40
00:02:50.108 --> 00:02:51.249
The vet came every day.

41
00:02:53.070 --> 00:02:57.312
John moved Ginger and Merrylegs into another part of the stable so I wouldn't be disturbed.

42
00:02:59.052 --> 00:03:01.333
Finally I got better, to everyone's relief.

43
00:03:03.593 --> 00:03:05.634
I could tell that Little Joe felt terrible.

44
00:03:06.814 --> 00:03:09.915
He'd learned his lesson, and he'd never make those mistakes again.

45
00:03:11.976 --> 00:03:14.496
John stayed angry with Little Joe for a long while.

46
00:03:17.617 --> 00:03:22.358
But as time passed and Joe kept trying to learn, John started to trust him again.

47
00:03:24.439 --> 00:03:27.580
One day the squire needed to send a note to a neighboring estate.

48
00:03:29.868 --> 00:03:32.950
John was out, so the squire told Little Joe to saddle me.

49
00:03:32.970 --> 00:03:37.752
"I know you haven't ridden much," he told Little Joe.

50
00:03:37.772 --> 00:03:40.254
"But Beauty will take care of you.

51
00:03:40.834 --> 00:03:42.535
Just ride carefully and you'll be fine."

52
00:03:45.276 --> 00:03:48.458
Little Joe wasn't a skilled rider, but he was gentle and careful.

53
00:03:49.599 --> 00:03:51.820
We delivered the note, then started for home.

54
00:03:55.182 --> 00:03:56.882
On the way we passed a muddy field.

55
00:03:58.043 --> 00:03:59.484
A two-horse cart was stuck there.

56
00:04:00.540 --> 00:04:02.381
It was piled high with heavy bricks.

57
00:04:03.983 --> 00:04:06.925
The driver was yelling and whipping his two horses again and again.

58
00:04:09.526 --> 00:04:11.007
Little Joe brought me to a halt.

59
00:04:12.188 --> 00:04:13.869
"Stop beating those horses!"

60
00:04:14.210 --> 00:04:14.790
he called.

61
00:04:14.810 --> 00:04:18.312
"They can't move the cart with all those bricks in it.

62
00:04:19.113 --> 00:04:20.654
The wheels are stuck in the mud!"

63
00:04:21.995 --> 00:04:22.976
The man ignored him.

64
00:04:24.096 --> 00:04:25.637
He lashed the horses once more.

65
00:04:25.657 --> 00:04:27.879
"Please stop!"

66
00:04:28.239 --> 00:04:29.080
Little Joe cried.

67
00:04:30.028 --> 00:04:31.489
"I'll help you unload some bricks.

68
00:04:32.169 --> 00:04:33.910
Maybe then they can pull out the cart."

69
00:04:33.930 --> 00:04:37.272
"Mind your own business!"

70
00:04:37.692 --> 00:04:38.413
the man yelled.

71
00:04:39.974 --> 00:04:41.174
Little Joe turned me around.

72
00:04:41.194 --> 00:04:44.476
"Come on, Beauty," he whispered.

73
00:04:44.496 --> 00:04:49.479
"We'd better tell that man's boss what's going on before he kills those horses."

74
00:04:51.060 --> 00:04:52.161
He kicked me into a gallop.

75
00:04:54.482 --> 00:04:58.024
We raced to the brickmaker's house, and Little Joe told him what was happening.

76
00:04:59.244 --> 00:05:01.565
"Thanks for letting me know," the brickmaker said.

77
00:05:01.585 --> 00:05:03.766
"I'll put a stop to it right now."

78
00:05:05.707 --> 00:05:08.948
When we got home, John could see that Little Joe looked angry.

79
00:05:10.529 --> 00:05:13.630
He asked what was wrong, and Little Joe told him the whole story.

80
00:05:18.172 --> 00:05:20.413
done," John said when the boy had finished.

81
00:05:20.433 --> 00:05:24.114
"Many people would have ridden past and not done anything.

82
00:05:25.155 --> 00:05:28.336
But it's everybody's business to put a stop to cruelty when they see it."

83
00:05:29.820 --> 00:05:32.762
Little Joe looked shy and proud of himself at the same time.

84
00:05:34.163 --> 00:05:35.944
After that there was something different about him.

85
00:05:37.585 --> 00:05:40.847
John said it was as if the boy had grown an inch taller that day.

86
00:05:41.627 --> 00:05:42.548
I believe it was true.
